{
  "env": {
    "BRIDGE_PORT_FILE": "bridge_udp.json",
    "FLMCP_AGENT_PROJECT": "FLMCP_AGENT_PROJECT",
    "FLMCP_FL_LICENSE": [
      "licensed",
      "trial"
    ],
    "FLMCP_KERNEL_ROOT": "FLMCP_KERNEL_ROOT",
    "FLMCP_SPOOL_ROOT": "FLMCP_SPOOL_ROOT",
    "bridge_port_file_schema": {
      "description": "Endpoint published by the native Bridge in each session spool.",
      "properties": {
        "pid": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Pid"
        },
        "port": {
          "maximum": 65535,
          "minimum": 1,
          "title": "Port",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "proto": {
          "title": "Proto",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "token": {
          "maxLength": 32,
          "minLength": 32,
          "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]+$",
          "title": "Token",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "transport": {
          "default": 1,
          "title": "Transport",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "proto",
        "port",
        "token"
      ],
      "title": "BridgePortFile",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "errors": {
    "categories": [
      "concurrent_write",
      "control_plane_unavailable",
      "control_plane_busy",
      "note_plane_unavailable",
      "invalid_argument",
      "internal_error",
      "unknown_target",
      "fl_api_error",
      "kernel_unavailable",
      "unsupported_in_live_session",
      "render_failed",
      "stale_handle",
      "operation_unsafe",
      "fl_relaunch_required",
      "file_lane_requires_reload",
      "fl_trial_unsupported",
      "unsupported_fl_build"
    ],
    "delivery": "ToolErrorResult JSON is delivered as the text content of isError tool results.",
    "shape": {
      "properties": {
        "candidates": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "items": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "type": "array"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Candidates"
        },
        "error": {
          "title": "Error",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "fix": {
          "title": "Fix",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "message": {
          "title": "Message",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "retryable": {
          "title": "Retryable",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "status": {
          "const": "error",
          "default": "error",
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "error",
        "message",
        "fix",
        "retryable"
      ],
      "title": "ToolErrorResult",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "description": "Run a Python cell in a persistent kernel bound to the live FL Studio\nsession, like a Jupyter notebook. Variables, imports, and functions persist\nacross calls. It is full Python: import anything, use files, numpy,\ntime.sleep, type/dir/getattr. `%pip install pkg` (or `!pip install pkg`)\ninstalls a package for later imports; `!cmd` runs a shell command. The\nworking directory is your workspace, the one place you can write; its files\nlast for the session. Pre-bound: fl (the SDK), theory, Note,\nAutomationPoint. A trailing expression is repr'd like a REPL.\n\nReturns {\"outcome\", \"stdout\", \"result\" | \"traceback\"}; stdout includes\nstderr. outcome is \"ok\", or \"error\" (read the traceback and fix the code),\nor \"interrupted\" when the cell ran past its 300 s budget (time inside fl\ncalls does not count) - the kernel and its variables are intact, or \"kernel_lost\" when\nthe kernel process died or was killed (os._exit, a crash, or ignoring the\ninterrupt) - its variables are gone, files stay, the next run starts fresh.\n\nHow the session behaves: every fl call applies to FL immediately and\nreturns once FL has it, or raises with the reason. A read right after a\nwrite returns the written notes; there is nothing to wait for, save, or\nreopen. To hear the result, render.\n\nThe SDK (no introspection needed):\n- fl.set_tempo(140.0) -> the tempo FL now has; fl.tempo reads it.\n- fl.channels -> [Channel(index, name), ...].\n- fl.track(\"Bass\") / fl.track(2, pattern=1) -> Track (exact name, index, or\n  unique substring; pattern defaults to 1).\n- Track.write([Note(...), ...], mode=\"merge\"|\"replace\") -> WriteResult(wrote,\n  track, pattern, mode, total): \"merge\" adds the notes, \"replace\" swaps the\n  pattern's notes on that track; total is how many it now has.\n  Track.notes() -> the notes it has now; Track.clear() empties it.\n- Note(key=60 or \"C4\"/\"F#3\", start=0.0, length=1.0, velocity=0.8, pan=0.5)\n  with start/length in beats from pattern start.\n- Track.set_channel_levels(volume=0.9, pan=-0.15, pitch=0) - volume 0..1,\n  pan -1..1, pitch whole semitones -48..48; returns FL's values.\n- Track.params(query=\"cutoff\") / Track.set_param(\"cutoff\", 0.55) - the\n  instrument's parameters, values normalized 0..1.\n- fl.render(\"mix.wav\") -> Path of the WAV. Only the file name is used: it\n  lands in the session's renders folder, which you can read but not write.\n  fl.analyze(path) -> bpm/key/LUFS/spectral balance; fl.read_wav(path) ->\n  (samples: numpy.ndarray, sample_rate: int).\n  A render plays the song in real time (FL's loop mode decides: the\n  playlist in song mode, only the selected pattern in pattern mode), so\n  render once when the pass is done; the harness listens back after you\n  say you are done. To check notes and tempo, use get_notes/get_scene\n  (instant) instead.\n- fl.snapshot() -> tempo + channels.\n- During a match FL is never reopened: fl.save() is not needed (and a\n  trial FL cannot save), and Track.set_automation, fl.add_effect and\n  fl.file_edit() are unavailable because they rewrite the saved song.\n- theory.chord(\"C\", \"minor\") / theory.scale(\"E\", \"minor\") -> MIDI ints;\n  theory.drums(\"x...x...x...x...\", key=\"C1\", step_beats=0.25) -> a\n  ready-to-write [Note] step grid ('x' = hit, '.' = rest).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "code": {
            "title": "Code",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "code"
        ],
        "title": "runArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "run",
      "outputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "outcome": {
            "enum": [
              "ok",
              "error",
              "interrupted",
              "kernel_lost"
            ],
            "title": "Outcome",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "result": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Result"
          },
          "stdout": {
            "title": "Stdout",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "traceback": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Traceback"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "outcome",
          "stdout"
        ],
        "title": "RunResult",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "The notes on one channel's pattern as FL has them now, including every\nwrite made this session. A list when small, a summary when large.\n\n``channel`` is an index; for a channel by name use run with\nfl.track(\"Lead\").notes().",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "channel": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "string"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Channel"
          },
          "pattern": {
            "title": "Pattern",
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "pattern",
          "channel"
        ],
        "title": "get_notesArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "get_notes",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "Note": {
            "description": "One note, in musical units. C4 = MIDI 60 = middle C.\n\n``key`` is firmly an int after construction: \"C4\"/\"F#3\" are accepted as\ninput and resolved once by ``pitch.parse_key``. Use ``pitch.key_name`` for\ndisplay. No downstream code ever sees a union.",
            "properties": {
              "color": {
                "default": 0,
                "maximum": 15,
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Color",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "key": {
                "maximum": 127,
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Key",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "length": {
                "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                "maximum": 1024,
                "title": "Length",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "pan": {
                "default": 0.5,
                "maximum": 1,
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Pan",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "start": {
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Start",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "velocity": {
                "default": 0.8,
                "maximum": 1,
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Velocity",
                "type": "number"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "key",
              "start",
              "length"
            ],
            "title": "Note",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "NotesSummary": {
            "properties": {
              "keys": {
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "propertyNames": {
                  "enum": [
                    "min",
                    "max"
                  ]
                },
                "title": "Keys",
                "type": "object"
              },
              "note": {
                "title": "Note",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "sample": {
                "items": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/Note"
                },
                "title": "Sample",
                "type": "array"
              },
              "span_beats": {
                "additionalProperties": {
                  "type": "number"
                },
                "propertyNames": {
                  "enum": [
                    "start",
                    "end"
                  ]
                },
                "title": "Span Beats",
                "type": "object"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "keys",
              "span_beats",
              "sample",
              "note"
            ],
            "title": "NotesSummary",
            "type": "object"
          },
          "Target": {
            "description": "A pattern/channel coordinate. Firmly ints: channel names and the\n\"current\" default are resolved AT THE TOOL BOUNDARY (server/sdk), never\ncarried as a union or a -1 sentinel into the core.",
            "properties": {
              "channel": {
                "minimum": 0,
                "title": "Channel",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "pattern": {
                "minimum": 1,
                "title": "Pattern",
                "type": "integer"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "pattern",
              "channel"
            ],
            "title": "Target",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "note_count": {
            "title": "Note Count",
            "type": "integer"
          },
          "notes": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/Note"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Notes"
          },
          "summary": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "$ref": "#/$defs/NotesSummary"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null
          },
          "target": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/Target"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "target",
          "note_count"
        ],
        "title": "GetNotesResult",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Read what is in FL now - tempo, key, and what each channel has, including\nevery write made this session and the current live tempo.\n\nCall this before writing, so additions fit what is already there. It returns\nan analysis rather than a note dump: a 56-note project summarises to about\n20 tokens instead of ~960, and the summary answers the questions that\nactually get asked.\n\nArgs:\n    detail: \"summary\" (default) for tempo, inferred key and a per-channel\n        digest - note count, span in beats, register, pitch classes, and for\n        bass-register parts the root motion; channels with no notes are\n        listed as such. Use \"notes\" only when you need individual notes,\n        such as harmonising an existing line.\n    channel: With detail=\"notes\", limit to one channel index.\n\nReturns:\n    For \"summary\", a `summary` string is included that is already formatted\n    for reading. Key inference carries a confidence and can be wrong on\n    modal or chromatic material - treat \"low\" as \"no reliable key\".",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "channel": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Channel"
          },
          "detail": {
            "default": "summary",
            "title": "Detail",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "title": "get_sceneArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "get_scene",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "SceneNote": {
            "properties": {
              "channel": {
                "title": "Channel",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "key": {
                "title": "Key",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "length": {
                "title": "Length",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "midi": {
                "title": "Midi",
                "type": "integer"
              },
              "start": {
                "title": "Start",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "velocity": {
                "title": "Velocity",
                "type": "number"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "channel",
              "key",
              "midi",
              "start",
              "length",
              "velocity"
            ],
            "title": "SceneNote",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "description": "One object for both detail modes.\n\nMCP requires every tool's output schema to be an object, so a root-level\nunion (summary | notes) is not expressible: the SDK rejected its own\ntools/list result and no client could list tools. detail=\"summary\" fills\nthe summary fields; detail=\"notes\" fills ``notes``.",
        "properties": {
          "automations": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "type": "object"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Automations"
          },
          "channels": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "additionalProperties": true,
                  "type": "object"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Channels"
          },
          "key": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Key"
          },
          "key_confidence": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Key Confidence"
          },
          "note_count": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "integer"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Note Count"
          },
          "notes": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "items": {
                  "$ref": "#/$defs/SceneNote"
                },
                "type": "array"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Notes"
          },
          "playlist": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "additionalProperties": true,
                "type": "object"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Playlist"
          },
          "summary": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Summary"
          },
          "tempo": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Tempo"
          }
        },
        "title": "GetSceneResult",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Play the song once from its start and record the mix to a WAV: how to hear\nyour edits. FL's loop mode decides what plays: the playlist in song mode, the\nselected pattern in pattern mode. Returns {\"path\", \"wavBase64\", \"span\"}:\nwavBase64 is the WAV in base64 (omitted with a note past the size cap); span\nsays what played (source \"song\" or \"pattern\"), its live beats and tempo, and\nthe seconds recorded. A render takes about that long, ten minutes at most.\nCall analyze afterwards for measurements.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {},
        "title": "renderArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "render",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "RenderSpan": {
            "description": "How long a render played, read from FL live just before the recording.\n\n``source`` is what FL plays in its current loop mode: the playlist\n(``\"song\"``) or the selected pattern (``\"pattern\"``, numbered by\n``pattern``). ``beats`` is that live length and ``tempo_bpm`` FL's live\ntempo. ``seconds`` is the time played; the capture adds a short decay\ntail. The tempo is the one at render time, so a song that\nautomates its tempo is captured at that tempo's length.",
            "properties": {
              "beats": {
                "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                "title": "Beats",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "pattern": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Pattern"
              },
              "seconds": {
                "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                "title": "Seconds",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "source": {
                "enum": [
                  "song",
                  "pattern"
                ],
                "title": "Source",
                "type": "string"
              },
              "tempo_bpm": {
                "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
                "title": "Tempo Bpm",
                "type": "number"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "source",
              "beats",
              "tempo_bpm",
              "seconds"
            ],
            "title": "RenderSpan",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "note": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Note"
          },
          "path": {
            "title": "Path",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "span": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/RenderSpan"
          },
          "wavBase64": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Wavbase64"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path",
          "span"
        ],
        "title": "RenderResult",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Measure a rendered WAV: bpm, key, integrated LUFS, true peak, and\nspectral balance. ``wav`` defaults to the most recent render (rendering\nfresh if none exists yet).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {
          "wav": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "default": null,
            "title": "Wav"
          }
        },
        "title": "analyzeArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "analyze",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "SpectralBalance": {
            "description": "Mean-square level by conventional production bands, in dBFS.",
            "properties": {
              "high_dbfs": {
                "title": "High Dbfs",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "low_dbfs": {
                "title": "Low Dbfs",
                "type": "number"
              },
              "mid_dbfs": {
                "title": "Mid Dbfs",
                "type": "number"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "low_dbfs",
              "mid_dbfs",
              "high_dbfs"
            ],
            "title": "SpectralBalance",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "bpm": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "number"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Bpm"
          },
          "integrated_lufs": {
            "title": "Integrated Lufs",
            "type": "number"
          },
          "key": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string"
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "title": "Key"
          },
          "spectral_balance": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/SpectralBalance"
          },
          "true_peak_dbfs": {
            "title": "True Peak Dbfs",
            "type": "number"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "bpm",
          "key",
          "integrated_lufs",
          "true_peak_dbfs",
          "spectral_balance"
        ],
        "title": "AudioAnalysis",
        "type": "object"
      }
    },
    {
      "description": "Setup diagnostics for whoever runs this engine. Not needed to check your\nwork: edits apply immediately and reads return what FL has.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "properties": {},
        "title": "fl_doctorArguments",
        "type": "object"
      },
      "name": "fl_doctor",
      "outputSchema": {
        "$defs": {
          "PlaneStatus": {
            "properties": {
              "connected": {
                "title": "Connected",
                "type": "boolean"
              },
              "detail": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Detail"
              },
              "fix": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Fix"
              },
              "fl_pid": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "integer"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Fl Pid"
              },
              "fl_pid_alive": {
                "anyOf": [
                  {
                    "type": "boolean"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "null"
                  }
                ],
                "default": null,
                "title": "Fl Pid Alive"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "connected"
            ],
            "title": "PlaneStatus",
            "type": "object"
          }
        },
        "properties": {
          "control_plane": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PlaneStatus"
          },
          "note_plane": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PlaneStatus"
          },
          "project_file": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/PlaneStatus"
          },
          "status": {
            "enum": [
              "ok",
              "degraded"
            ],
            "title": "Status",
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "status",
          "control_plane",
          "note_plane",
          "project_file"
        ],
        "title": "DoctorReport",
        "type": "object"
      }
    }
  ],
  "version": "0.1.0"
}
